  "content": {
    "title": "Gonzaga vs Texas score, results: Longhorns upset Bulldogs, head to Sweet 16",
    "text": "Updated March 21, 2026, 10:45 p.m. ETFollow all of Saturday's NCAA Tournament second round games with USA TODAY Sports' live updates.No. 11 seed Texas pulled off the 74-68 upset against No. 3 seed Gonzaga on Saturday night. The Longhorns had lost five of their last six games heading into the NCAA Tournament, but the team remains on a heater heading to the Sweet 16.Matas Vokietaitis nearly produced a double-double with 17 points and nine rebounds for the Longhorns. Jordon Pope also scored 17 points in the victory.Texas beat NC State in the First Four and upset No. 6 BYU despite AJ Dybantsa going for 35 points.Gonzaga needed to dig deep to get past No. 14 seed Kennesaw State in Thursday's first round and couldn’t do it again in the second round.Graham Ike scored 25 points for the Bulldogs. Gonzaga's struggles from the three-point line continued, making just 4-of-16 shots from long range.Here's what you need to know from today's second round matchup with a spot in next week's Sweet 16 going to Texas: Final: Texas 74, Gonzaga 68The score between the Longhorns and the Bulldogs remained close throughout the second half, but it was Texas who outscored Gonzaga 39-35 in the period. Texas and Gonzaga continue to battleThe Bulldogs and the Longhorns have continued to exchange leads throughout the second half. Texas leads Gonzaga 49-47 with 11:43 left in the second half. Both teams have scored 14 total points.Matas Vokietaitis and Jordan Pope have scored 11 points each for the Longhorns. Graham Ike has scored 15 points for the Bulldogs so far. Halftime: Texas 35, Gonzaga 33Gonzaga led by as many as eight points in the first half, but it was Texas who carried a lead into the locker room. The Longhorns never led by more than two points in the first half.Jordan Pope scored nine of the Longhorns' 35 points in the first half. He shot 4-of-9 from the field and 1-for-4 from the three-point line. Matas Vokietaitis produced seven points and four rebounds.Jalen Warley has produced seven points and five rebounds for the Bulldogs. Gonzaga leads Texas early in first halfThe Bulldogs lead the Longhorns 18-15 with 9:37 left in the first half. Graham Ike led Gonzaga with six points while Emmanuel Innocenti added four points. Daily Swain leads Texas with five points. The teams are shooting a combined 1-for-10 from the three-point line. Gonzaga vs Texas live scoreTEAMS1H2HFTexas353974Gonzaga333568What time is Gonzaga vs Texas?Time: 7:10 p.m. ET, Saturday.What channel is Gonzaga vs Texas? How to watch, streaming infoThe game is airing on TBS/truTV, stream via Fubo.Gonzaga vs Texas prediction, oddsEhsan Kassim: TexasJordan Mendoza: GonzagaJohn Leuzzi: TexasBlake Schuster: TexasMoneyline: Gonzaga (-250); Texas (+200)Spread: Gonzaga (-6.5)Over/under total: 146.5Gonzaga NCAA Tournament history (since 2014)Appearances: 12Most recent appearance: 2026Games played: 42 (30-11)Highest seed: 1Lowest seed: 11Deepest round reached: National Championship",
